title: The boiler, in that order
story: fernhill
description: The state machine on the boiler — FILL, PRIME, LIGHT — and what it
  says when the order is wrong. Also the crate's tool gate, unopened.

seed: 1

---

> north
[OK: contains "Gravel Drive"]

> north
[OK: contains "Fountain Court"]

> east
[OK: contains "Boiler Shed"]
[OK: contains "You can see a nailed crate and a furnace poker here"]

# The brass plate is the instruction sheet for the machine below.
> examine the boiler
[OK: contains "FILL. PRIME. LIGHT. IN THAT ORDER"]

# LIGHT out of order, from `cold`. `on switching_on it` refuses before the
# machine's `when switching_on the furnace: running` transition can be reached.
> switch on the boiler
[OK: contains "a hollow CLANK, like church bells dropped down a well"]
[OK: not contains "hums to life"]

# PRIME out of order. The plunger's own refusal replaces the action's text —
# note there is no "You push the primer plunger." line here, and there is one
# below once the jacket is full.
> push the primer plunger
[OK: contains "Nothing to prime — the jacket is empty"]
[OK: not contains "You push the primer plunger"]

# The crate is `openable with the crowbar`, and the crowbar is in the Cellar.
# Tool gates report the need without naming the tool.
> open the nailed crate
[OK: contains "You need something to open the nailed crate with"]
[EVENT: false, type="if.event.opened"]

# FILL. `state cold / when turning the stopcock: filled`, and the entering
# state's `on enter` is what speaks.
> turn the stopcock
[OK: contains "You crank the stopcock a hard quarter-turn"]
[OK: contains "water gurgles down into the jacket"]

# LIGHT still out of order — `filled` is not `primed`, and the refusal is the
# same line, which is the story's point: the boiler has one complaint.
> switch on the boiler
[OK: contains "a hollow CLANK, like church bells dropped down a well"]

# PRIME, in order this time. The default action text now survives.
> push the primer plunger
[OK: contains "You push the primer plunger"]
[OK: contains "The plunger meets resistance at last and thumps home"]

# LIGHT, in order. The terminal state warms the pipes and, at a distance,
# moves the vine from `seedling` to `flowering` in a room the player is not in.
> switch on the boiler
[OK: contains "The boiler hums to life"]
[OK: contains "Flame catches with a soft whump"]
[OK: contains "At the warm end of the greenhouse staging, something green stirs"]

# `score lit worth 10` takes the total to 10 and promotes the rank.
[OK: contains "The house has stopped listening for your footsteps"]

# `on taking it while the boiler is running` — the poker was takeable a moment
# ago and is not any more.
> take the furnace poker
[OK: contains "it would take the skin off your palm"]
[EVENT: false, type="if.event.taken"]

> score
[OK: contains "You have scored 10 out of 50"]
[OK: contains "Guest of the House"]
